# eirl-storage-eject: `eirl-storage eject` in the system's mount namespace (RECORDING.md §4). The app runs
# `sudo eirl-storage eject` (an exact sudoers rule), which starts this unit and returns its exit status: run inside the
# app's sandbox (ProtectSystem=strict, PrivateTmp) the unmount would only happen in the app's own mount namespace and the
# state could not be written. No sandboxing here for the same reason. Not enabled: nothing starts it but the helper.
[Unit]
Description=eirl-storage: eject the USB disk of local recordings
Documentation=https://github.com/enhanced-irl/eirl-encoder/blob/main/RECORDING.md

[Service]
Type=oneshot
Environment=EIRL_STORAGE_DIRECT=1
ExecStart=/usr/local/sbin/eirl-storage eject
TimeoutStartSec=120
